---
args: { prepared: PreparedEvidence, goal: GoalContract, policy: PolicySelection }
returns: DecisionAtom[]
---
Apply this domain algorithm to prepared evidence: Propose conventional and inventive matches based on function rather than product names. Explain the adaptation mechanism and uncertainty, include multi-item bundles when useful, and reject creativity that depends on relaxing essential requirements or unapproved handling.
For each field, return a value only when supported, source IDs, authority, one rejected alternative, and status established, disputed, unknown, or inapplicable. Preserve contrary evidence and distinguish observation from inference.
